<!-- The M.D. Ala. bankruptcy motion's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs)
     in the face of the typst template ({font}, Times New Roman) at 12 pt (size 24 half points, matched to the adversary complaint in this court;
     no local rule sets a size); Body Text in exact 24 pt line boxes (typst pitch-double, double-spaced by convention)
     with a half-inch indent, and the headings in them; single lines in 13.8 pt boxes (typst pitch-single); letter
     page with 1-inch margins. The footer (rIdFtrDash) is the typst one: "-N-" centered at 11 pt in a 12.65 pt line
     box, the line 37.75 pt above the page foot (755 twips: where typst sets it, footer-descent 30 %).
     docx/almb-motion-brief.lua writes every paragraph's own spacing. Twips: 20 x pt. -->
